message: >-
  This is an AI-produced draft, not reviewed by a specialist, and it should not be
  cited as scholarship until it has been reviewed. If you refer to it, give the
  version you read and the date you read it, and say that it is an unreviewed draft.
  How to cite a square or a passage: see "How to cite" in README.md.
title: "Filosofía cortesana: a playable edition"
version: "0.2"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
abstract: >-
  A playable web edition of Alonso de Barros's Filosofía cortesana (Madrid 1587;
  Naples 1588), the earliest known themed Game of the Goose, on Mario Cartaro's
  board of 1588 (British Museum 1869,0410.2463.+). It gives a transcription and
  English translation of the Naples 1588 book, the passages of the Madrid 1587
  (Pedro Madrigal) edition absent from it, the recorded readings of the first
  edition, and annotations on every square and figure of the board. Version 0.2,
  October 2026: an AI-produced draft, not reviewed by a specialist.
keywords:
  - Alonso de Barros
  - Filosofía cortesana
  - Game of the Goose
  - Mario Cartaro
  - court of Philip II
  - digital edition
